00:37:41,000 --> 00:37:43,160
哎，那我倒是不介意接手，
我正好有台唱片机。
Well, I wouldn't mind,
I've got a record player.

692
00:37:43,200 --> 00:37:46,400
我挺喜欢那动静……
[模仿唱片搓盘声]
I like that...
[IMITATES RECORD SCRATCHING]

693
00:37:46,440 --> 00:37:48,120
-每首歌里都能听到的那种打碟杂音。
-行啊，刚才那段……
-That you get to
accompany all the songs.
-Well, that now...

694
00:37:48,160 --> 00:37:49,440
刚才那段说唱还挺带感，
That was a good rap track,

695
00:37:49,480 --> 00:37:51,440
相当地道的嘻哈味儿，你直接……
it was a very good
hip hop track, you just...

696
00:37:51,480 --> 00:37:53,880
-哎别说，你完全能发出来。
-那我可得去申请专利了。
-Oh, no, you could
put that out.
-I'll copyright that.

697
00:37:53,920 --> 00:37:58,400
你现在把它挂到iTunes上，
有人下载你就能净赚79便士。
You could put that on iTunes
now and make 79p from someone
downloading it.

698
00:37:58,440 --> 00:38:01,040
不过说实话，
咱俩现在听起来像极了两个牢骚满腹的糟老头子。
We do sound like
a couple of grumpy old men,
though, to be honest.

699
00:38:01,080 --> 00:38:02,800
我本来就是个爱发牢骚的糟老头子。
I am a grumpy
old man, really.

700
00:38:02,840 --> 00:38:04,720
-还真是，前阵子咱俩都上过《牢骚老头》那节目。
-没错。
-Well we are, we both appeared
in it, quite recently.
-Yes.

701
00:38:04,760 --> 00:38:07,480
那你最近又看什么不顺眼了？
还是那些烦人的宣传口号吗？
What's the latest
thing you've got?
Is it slogans you don't like?

702
00:38:07,520 --> 00:38:09,800
哎，我在《牢骚老头》上
吐槽过的一件事，
Well, one of the things
I moaned about on
Grumpy Old Men

703
00:38:09,840 --> 00:38:13,800
也是我至今耿耿于怀的，就是现在每家公司……
which I feel very strongly
about is that every company...

704
00:38:13,840 --> 00:38:16,640
我是说，
每个地方议会、
议会的每个下属部门……
I mean,
every council,
every Branch of Parliament...

705
00:38:16,680 --> 00:38:19,360
-所有单位。
-每个人非得整一句口号不可。
-Everybody.
-Everybody has to
have a slogan.

706
00:38:19,400 --> 00:38:21,440
要我说最扯淡的就是英国皇家汽车俱乐部（RAC），
The worst one,
I think, is the RAC,

707
00:38:21,480 --> 00:38:25,320
因为他们现在的口号是：
“时刻在那（Always there）。”
because their slogan is now,
"Always there."

708
00:38:25,360 --> 00:38:27,560
可“那儿”恰恰是你最不希望他们在的地方！
And that's the one place
you don't want them to be.

709
00:38:27,600 --> 00:38:29,440
[杰里米笑声]
[JEREMY LAUGHING]

710
00:38:29,480 --> 00:38:32,880
每次我车抛锚、
或者需要救援的时候，
我都希望他们“在这儿”！
Whenever my car breaks down,
or I need the RAC
I want them here.

711
00:38:32,920 --> 00:38:34,760
我才不要他们“在那儿”呢！
I don't want them there.

712
00:38:34,800 --> 00:38:36,520
不，我最恶心的一句……
No, my least favourite...

713
00:38:36,560 --> 00:38:38,120
前几天我出去散步时
正好看到过这么一个标语。
I saw one of
these the other day
when I was out for a walk.

714
00:38:38,160 --> 00:38:39,840
我知道，这完全不符合我的作风。
Strange thing for me
to be doing, I know.

715
00:38:39,880 --> 00:38:41,600
但那块立在路边的路标上写着……
But it said
on this signpost...

716
00:38:41,640 --> 00:38:43,480
荒郊野岭的，不知哪个好事者立的。
Countryside, somebody
would have put it up.

717
00:38:43,520 --> 00:38:46,720
-“除了时间，什么都别消磨（杀）。”
-[赖斯笑声]
-"Kill nothing, only time."
-[RICE LAUGHING]

718
00:38:46,760 --> 00:38:48,720
简直一股苏联味儿！
That's just Soviet.

719
00:38:48,760 --> 00:38:51,160
因为当年苏联的拖拉机制造厂里
就老贴这种标语，
'Cause they used
to have that kind of thing
in Soviet tractor factories

720
00:38:51,200 --> 00:38:53,040
专门用来催工人拼命干活！
to get people to work harder.

721
00:38:53,080 --> 00:38:56,440
我觉得所有的宣传标语，
各种形式的口号，
I think every slogan,
every logo type slogan

722
00:38:56,480 --> 00:38:59,560
骨子里其实都在传达一句话：
“对你管东管西。”
really is saying the same
thing: "Bossing you about."

723
00:38:59,600 --> 00:39:01,280
因为你看嘛，
现在你什么都不准干。
'Cause, you know,
you're not allowed
to do anything now.

724
00:39:01,320 --> 00:39:03,120
开车不准超过时速70英里，
Drive over 70 miles an hour,

725
00:39:03,160 --> 00:39:06,680
不准去捉螃蟹，
不准玩栗子大战，或者……
or catch crabs
or play conkers, or...

726
00:39:06,720 --> 00:39:08,800
不，就是捉海蟹，
别瞎想。
No, catch crabs.
Those sorts.

727
00:39:08,840 --> 00:39:12,240
还偷笑！
不，这种社会风气真是绝了。
Sniggering!
No, it's an
extraordinary culture.

728
00:39:12,280 --> 00:39:14,360
你什么都干不了。
Nothing you can do.

729
00:39:14,400 --> 00:39:18,960
而且我知道你平时总花时间
琢磨的一件事，
就是死亡。
And one of the things I know
that you spend your time
thinking about is dying.

730
00:39:19,000 --> 00:39:21,520
-呃，恐怕还真是。
-这是真的，千真万确。
-Well, yes, I'm afraid.
-It's true, this, it's true.

731
00:39:21,560 --> 00:39:23,440
因为之前我在一家报纸上
写过一篇关于死亡的专栏，
Because I wrote
a piece about it in
one of the newspapers

732
00:39:23,480 --> 00:39:25,600
结果你居然给我写信说：
“我也老琢磨这事儿。”
and you actually
wrote to me saying,
"I do that as well."

733
00:39:25,640 --> 00:39:28,160
哎，你几乎所有的专栏文章
都让我深受触动，
Well, I am deeply moved
by nearly all your columns,

734
00:39:28,200 --> 00:39:30,000
-如果可以这么说的话，呃……
-[清嗓子]
-if I may put it
that way, um...
-[CLEARS THROAT]

735
00:39:30,040 --> 00:39:32,120
[众人大笑]
[ALL LAUGHING]

736
00:39:32,160 --> 00:39:34,120
-绝大多数专栏吧。而且……
-[轻笑]
-Most of your columns.
And...
-[CHUCKLES]

737
00:39:34,160 --> 00:39:36,240
我觉得要是真得走……
I think if we're going
to go...

738
00:39:36,280 --> 00:39:39,360
罗杰·麦高夫在一首叫
《年轻人的死法》的诗里总结得妙极了。
Roger McGough summed it up
brilliantly in a poem called
Young Man's Death.

739
00:39:39,400 --> 00:39:41,800
他想活到90岁再死，
And he wanted to die
age 90, but he wanted

740
00:39:41,840 --> 00:39:43,960
但他希望死得像个年轻人，
to die a young man's
death of being

741
00:39:44,000 --> 00:39:48,720
比如被情妇吃醋的丈夫
当场活活打死。
beaten up by, you know,
his lover's jealous partner.

742
00:39:48,760 --> 00:39:53,360
不，我想在报废的核反应堆里
跟老虎决斗战死。
No, I want to go fighting
a tiger in a broken
nuclear reactor.

743
00:39:53,400 --> 00:39:56,200
我希望那能成为一段传奇，
要够刺激，
I want it to be an anecdote.
I want something exciting,

744
00:39:56,240 --> 00:39:58,200
能让你稳稳登上头版头条的那种。
something that gets you
on the front pages.

745
00:39:58,240 --> 00:40:00,360
-对，但现在还不行。
-你还没准备好？
-Yes, but not yet.
-You're not ready yet?

746
00:40:00,400 --> 00:40:03,880
-我还没准备好呢。
-因为今天你要是在赛道上，
-I'm not ready yet.
-'Cause if you'd gone out on
the track today, of course

747
00:40:03,920 --> 00:40:06,600
把车给撞了个稀巴烂，
那绝对妥妥是头条新闻。
and crashed the car,
that would have
been a front page story.

748
00:40:06,640 --> 00:40:08,560
确实会，
不知道标题会怎么写。
Yes, it would have been.
I wonder what it would
have said.

749
00:40:08,600 --> 00:40:10,200
我是说，我……
I mean, I was on...

750
00:40:10,240 --> 00:40:11,640
我是说，肯定会写：
“《贝隆夫人》词作者身亡。”
I mean, it would have said
"Evitaman dies."

751
00:40:11,680 --> 00:40:14,640
或者“劳埃德·韦伯的搭档去世”，
全是这种让人抓狂的标题。
Or "Lloyd Webber partner dies"
or something really annoying.

752
00:40:14,680 --> 00:40:17,200
-我的意思是……
-[众人大笑]
-I mean...
-[ALL LAUGHING]

753
00:40:17,240 --> 00:40:19,280
话说回来，你可算不上什么车迷。
Now, petrol head you are not.

754
00:40:19,320 --> 00:40:21,160
你现在开的是什么车？
What car do you have now?

755
00:40:21,200 --> 00:40:23,640
-一辆捷豹。
-[笑声]
其实我知道……
-It's a Jag.
-[LAUGHING]
Actually, I know...

756
00:40:23,680 --> 00:40:25,680
而且是灰色的。
And it's grey.

757
00:40:25,720 --> 00:40:27,160
前几天我们的调研员
给他办公室打电话，
Our researchers
rung up the office,
his office, the other day,

758
00:40:27,200 --> 00:40:29,840
问：“到底是什么车？”
对方答：“捷豹X什么来着。”
and said, "What is it?"
"It's an X something."

759
00:40:29,880 --> 00:40:31,640
你现在搞清楚到底是哪款了吗？
Have you found out
what it is yet?

760
00:40:31,680 --> 00:40:34,760
我就知道你会问，
可我又给忘了，
反正就是X什么玩意儿。
I knew you'd ask,
and I've forgotten it.
It's an X something.

761
00:40:34,800 --> 00:40:37,040
那是辆捷豹X-Type，XJS……
It's a Jaguar X type, XJS...

762
00:40:37,080 --> 00:40:38,680
是辆轿车，
里面有四个座。
It's a saloon.
It's got four seats in it.

763
00:40:38,720 --> 00:40:40,480
挺好。
Very good.

764
00:40:40,520 --> 00:40:42,560
-收音机很棒，空调也猛得很。
-收音机确实棒。
-Great radio and terrific
air conditioning.
-Great radio.

765
00:40:42,600 --> 00:40:46,280
你开车总喜欢
一边吹着冷气，
一边开着座椅加热。
You always drive
with the air conditioning
and the seat heater on.

766
00:40:46,320 --> 00:40:49,040
这组合挺怪的。
我建议你试试，
其实相当刺激销魂。
It's a strange combination.
I recommend you try it.
It's rather erotic.

767
00:40:49,080 --> 00:40:54,200
你那儿会有一股……
一股热浪直往你
下半身涌，
You have a heat...
Heat pulsating
up your parts

768
00:40:54,240 --> 00:40:56,280
可身上其他地方又冷得要命。
and it's cold everywhere else.

769
00:40:56,320 --> 00:40:58,520
肯定就像……
我是说……
Must about...
I mean...

770
00:40:58,560 --> 00:41:01,240
很显然，爱斯基摩人看《海滩救护队》之类节目时
大概就是这种感觉。
Obviously, it's how Eskimos
must feel when watching
Baywatchor something.

771
00:41:01,280 --> 00:41:03,160
-我不知道，这……呃……
-[克拉克森轻笑]
-I don't know, it's, uh...
-[CLARKSON CHUCKLES]

772
00:41:03,200 --> 00:41:06,120
对我来说座椅加热
主要是用来……
悄悄给副驾打开……
Seat heaters for me are
something that you turn on...
Your passenger's on...

773
00:41:06,160 --> 00:41:08,120
-趁他们不留神，“快看那边！”
-没错。
-When they're not...
"Look at that."
-Yes.

774
00:41:08,160 --> 00:41:10,720
然后你就等着，因为你懂的，
过了两分钟他们就会喊：“哎呀完了，
And then you wait, 'cause,
you know, in two minutes
they go, "Oh, no,

775
00:41:10,760 --> 00:41:14,240
“我裤子……我尿裤子了！天呐！””
"I've had an accident
in my... Oh, no!"

776
00:41:14,280 --> 00:41:15,760
言归正传，来看你的圈速。
Anyway, your lap.

777
00:41:15,800 --> 00:41:17,160
-玩得爽吗？
-爽爆了。
-Was it fun?
-Great fun.

778
00:41:17,200 --> 00:41:19,080
咱们来瞧瞧那一圈跑得如何？
Shall we have a look
at the lap?

779
00:41:19,120 --> 00:41:21,720
来看看他开得怎么样吧？
好，放录像。
走起！
Should we see how he did?
Okay, let's play the tape.
Here we go.

780
00:41:21,760 --> 00:41:24,720
[轮胎尖叫声]
[TYRES SQUEALING]

781
00:41:24,760 --> 00:41:28,040
克拉克森：刚才那是飙到了4500转
然后就……我的天！
CLARKSON: So was that
4,500 rpm and then just...
Oh, my word!

782
00:41:30,400 --> 00:41:31,720
赖斯：这会儿看着慢得要死，
RICE: It looks
terribly slow here,

783
00:41:31,760 --> 00:41:33,400
但我向你保证，
当时实际快得多。
but I promise you,
it was a lot faster.

784
00:41:33,440 --> 00:41:35,160
克拉克森：哎，这个弯过得够英勇。
CLARKSON: Well,
that's a good brave corner.

785
00:41:35,200 --> 00:41:37,080
你总觉得
自己要撞了，
You always think
you're going to crash

786
00:41:37,120 --> 00:41:39,040
但等你从另一侧切出去时，
其实从来没人真撞过。
when you come off
the other side
and nobody ever does.

787
00:41:39,080 --> 00:41:41,320
就是这股劲头。
[模仿引擎轰鸣声]
That was that power.
[IMITATING ENGINE]

788
00:41:41,360 --> 00:41:42,840
克拉克森：你踩到红线断油了。
CLARKSON: You hit
the rev limit.

789
00:41:42,880 --> 00:41:45,440
居然没蹭到轮胎墙，
不像斯提格。
You managed to miss the tyres,
unlike the Stig.

790
00:41:46,720 --> 00:41:49,720
-非常干净利落。
-对吧。
-Very neat and tidy.
-Right.

791
00:41:49,760 --> 00:41:52,840
-你以前真从没在机库或赛道上开过？
-一次都没。
-You've never driven
in a hangar or a track before?
-Never.

792
00:41:52,880 --> 00:41:55,120
那我不得不说，瞧瞧这个，
完了……哎，居然救回来了！
Well, I have to say,
look at that.
Oh, no. Oh, yes.

793
00:41:55,160 --> 00:41:58,040
这儿相当快，
差点把摄像师给报销了。
Quite fast there,
nearly got the cameraman.

794
00:41:58,760 --> 00:42:00,320
还有，呃，那是……
And, well, that's...

795
00:42:00,360 --> 00:42:02,560
-相当别致的新走线啊。
-新走线？
-Unusual new line.
-A new line?

796
00:42:02,600 --> 00:42:04,480
反正车又不是我的。
It's not my car.

797
00:42:04,520 --> 00:42:06,320
克拉克森：现在到了吓人的路段了。
CLARKSON: Now this
is the scary bit.

798
00:42:08,120 --> 00:42:11,400
纯爷们儿，全程大脚给油过弯，
再次切过轮胎堆。
Brave man, on the power
all the way round,
back through the tyres.

799
00:42:11,440 --> 00:42:12,920
又是一次，又毫发无伤避开了。
Again, missed them again.

800
00:42:12,960 --> 00:42:14,960
噢，现在看着才像真实速度嘛。
Oh, now that looks
like the real speed.

801
00:42:16,320 --> 00:42:19,560
噢，你看，
你这下有点……
哎呀，完蛋！
Oh, now,
you've got that a bit...
Oh, dear, no!

802
00:42:19,600 --> 00:42:22,120
天哪，老天爷啊。
Oh dear, oh, Lord.

803
00:42:22,160 --> 00:42:23,360
这下肯定要慢不少了。
That's gonna slow you
down a bit.

804
00:42:24,000 --> 00:42:26,040
换换花样嘛。
Makes a change.

805
00:42:26,080 --> 00:42:28,800
过了甘邦弯。
哎呀，在这儿损失了好多速度。
Around Gambon.
Oh, dear, we've lost
quite a lot of speed there.

806
00:42:28,840 --> 00:42:31,000
冲线了！
And there we are,
across the line.

807
00:42:43,080 --> 00:42:44,480
那你觉得自己能排第几？
Where do you reckon, then?

808
00:42:44,520 --> 00:42:47,160
鉴于你快到终点时冲出了赛道，
Bearing in mind that you did
go off toward the end,

809
00:42:47,200 --> 00:42:50,000
这肯定耽误了你不少时间。
which will have
slowed you down a bit.

810
00:42:50,040 --> 00:42:52,080
按我巅峰状态来看的话……
Well, I would have thought
at my peak...

811
00:42:52,120 --> 00:42:54,960
-其实那是1957年的事了。
-[杰里米轻笑]
-Actually, that was 1957.
-[JEREMY CHUCKLING]

812
00:42:55,000 --> 00:42:58,320
我想的是：“只要不是倒数第一就行。”
大家都这么说。
I would think,
"I'm hoping, I'm not last."
Everybody says that.

813
00:42:58,360 --> 00:43:01,520
我猜差不多是大卫·索尔那水平，1分54秒？
I would think David Soul,
that level, 1:54?

814
00:43:01,560 --> 00:43:04,080
1分54秒？不，
有个好消息能让你高兴高兴。
1:54? No,
I can cheer you up.

815
00:43:04,120 --> 00:43:06,120
-你比大卫·索尔还快。
-哇哦。
-You're faster
than David Soul.
-Wow.

816
00:43:06,160 --> 00:43:11,520
你的成绩是1分
52秒7。
You did it in one minute,
52.7 seconds.

817
00:43:11,560 --> 00:43:12,960
所以你排在……
So you are...

818
00:43:20,040 --> 00:43:23,000
和“神秘博士”一个水平。
The same kind of speed
as Dr Who.

819
00:43:23,040 --> 00:43:24,520
而且我还干掉了硬汉维尼·琼斯。
And I beat hard man
Vinnie Jones.

820
00:43:24,560 --> 00:43:27,080
你确实赢了硬汉。
